# The text of a table module of `unicode/encodings`: its header, which says
# what the table is, that this program made it and from which files, then
# its constants, a blank line between each, and a line feed at its end. And
# the record of the one fetch every header names: its day, `FETCHED`, and
# the bytes it brought, `FETCHED_SHA256`.

use <rebel>/strings

# The day the vendored files of `whatwg/` were read from
# encoding.spec.whatwg.org, which serves the Encoding Standard's resources at
# their latest version under the same names.
constant FETCHED: str
    "2026-11-22"

# Each file of `whatwg/`, one space, and the SHA-256 of its bytes as
# encoding.spec.whatwg.org served them on `FETCHED`, in lowercase
# hexadecimal, by the bytes of its name. The folder holds these files and no
# other, each byte for byte, before anything is read from one
# (`main.read_sources`): no edit, no file of another version and no file
# added reaches a table unseen. It is also what lets
# `tests/harness/suite_unseen.hero` leave the folder unread: the C1 controls,
# soft hyphens, marks and fillers a single-byte or Korean index maps a byte
# to are the standard's characters, written as themselves.
constant FETCHED_SHA256: [str]
    [
        "encodings.json 078212b3697f60b81225b6671bd9da2604497abff0aa8e96e4d46605c02ac9e7"
        "index-big5.txt 08e24270c8e95d998c994c03f907e972480dc01f58743e078654cc466203c8ff"
        "index-euc-kr.txt 89af20dd867c84cefb710b1790229786cfef2bf11916361a210d81b90381e267"
